{title: Yet Not I but Through Christ in Me}
{subtitle: Nur durch Christus in mir}
{song_number: 144}
{language: en}
{tempo: 75}
{key: C}

{start_of_verse: 1}
What gift of [C]grace is Jesus, my Re[F]deemer.
There is no [C]more for heaven [Am]now to [G]give.
He is my [C]joy, my righteousness and [F]freedom,
my steadfast [C]love, my deep and [Gsus4]boundless [G]peace. [C]
To this I [F]hold: my hope is only [C]Jesus.
For my [F]life is wholly bound to [Gsus4]his. [G]
Oh how [C]strange and di[Dm7]vine, I can [C/E]sing: all is [F]mine!
Yet not [C/G]I, but through [Gsus4]Christ [G]in [C]me.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 2}
The night is [C]dark, but I am not for[F]saken,
for by my [C]side the Saviour [Am]he will [G]stay.
I labour [C]on in weakness and re[F]joicing,
for in my [C]need, his power [Gsus4]is dis[G]played. [C]
To this I [F]hold: my Shepherd will de[C]fend me.
Through the [F]deepest valley he will [Gsus4]lead. [G]
Oh the [C]night has been [Dm7]won, and I [C/E]shall over[F]come!
Yet not [C/G]I, but through [Gsus4]Christ [G]in [C]me.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 3}
No fate I [C]dread, I know I am for[F]given,
the future [C]sure, the price, it [Am]has been [G]paid.
For Jesus [C]bled and suffered for my [F]pardon,
and he was [C]raised to over[Gsus4]throw the [G]grave. [C]
To this I [F]hold: my sin has been de[C]feated.
Jesus [F]now, and ever, is my [Gsus4]plea. [G]
Oh the [C]chains are re[Dm7]leased, I can [C/E]sing: I am [F]free!
Yet not [C/G]I, but through [Gsus4]Christ [G]in [C]me.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 4}
With ev'ry [C]breath I long to follow [F]Jesus,
for he has [C]said that he will [Am]bring me [G]home.
And day by [C]day I know he will re[F]new me
until I [C]stand with joy be[Gsus4]fore the [G]throne. [C]
To this I [F]hold: my hope is only [C]Jesus.
All the [F]glory evermore to [Gsus4]him. [G]
When the [C]race is com[Dm7]plete, still my [C/E]lips shall re[F]peat:
Yet not [C/G]I, but through [Gsus4]Christ [G]in [Am]me.
Yet not [F]I, but through [Gsus4]Christ [G]in [C]me.
